diff --git a/docs/ops/overview.md b/docs/ops/overview.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..0aa16db
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/ops/overview.md
@@ -0,0 +1,27 @@
+# Observability Lanes
+
+This project separates logs into three distinct *lanes* to keep operational concerns isolated and make troubleshooting easier.
+
+| Lane | Purpose | When to use |
+|------|---------|------------|
+| **Archive** | Routine application logs (`debug → error`). Stored daily, retained 14 days. | General debugging, normal operation, log‑driven metrics. |
+| **Audit** | Durable record of who did what. Stores actions such as role changes, subscription updates, failed login attempts, etc. | Any change that may be relevant for compliance, support or forensic analysis. |
+| **Alert** | Human‑pageable incidents. Sends a short message to Discord when something requires immediate attention. | Queue failures, webhook time‑outs, plan limits being hit, critical business logic failures. |
+
+Use the appropriate channel:
+
+```php
+use Illuminate\Support\Facades\Log;
+
+// Archive (default stack)
+Log::info('User logged in', ['user_id' => $id]);
+
+// Audit
+Log::channel('audit')->info('Subscription upgraded', ['user_id' => $id, 'plan' => $plan]);
+
+// Alert
+$discord = app(App\Ops\DiscordOpsAlert::class);
+$discord->send('Job failed', 'The payment webhook for user 42 timed out.', ['job_id' => $jobId]);
+```
+
+The `DiscordOpsAlert` service is a thin wrapper that formats the message and safely redacts sensitive data before posting to the configured webhook.
